%% Reader question: How can semantic recall improve discovery while versioned sources retain authority and enable poisoning recovery?
%% Evidence cutoff: 2026-07-11
%% Claim status: reference design; public memory-mcp repository mechanics are verified, end-to-end fleet enforcement and effectiveness are unverified
flowchart LR
    accTitle: Memory read, write, and rebuild flow
    accDescr: A caller authenticates and receives readable scopes before a read tries a known structured key or uses semantic search to discover candidates. Selected hits must carry provenance and resolve to an authoritative versioned source before use. A write updates an authoritative domain record before review and optional fleet promotion, then indexes the immutable revision. A correction changes the source, commits a minimized authoritative tombstone consumed by every rebuild, verifies deletion propagation, rebuilds a fresh index, compares it with the source manifest, and atomically promotes the verified index.

    subgraph READ["Read: discovery is not authority"]
      direction TB
      T["Caller identity and task"] --> AUTH["Authenticate and derive readable scopes"]
      AUTH --> K{"Known structured key?"}
      K -->|"Yes"| D["Deterministic source lookup"]
      K -->|"No"| S["Semantic candidate search in approved scopes"]
      S --> P{"Complete provenance and access?"}
      P -->|"No"| Q["Reject or quarantine hit"]
      P -->|"Yes"| A["Resolve immutable authoritative source"]
      D --> A
      A --> V["Verify revision, supersession, privacy, and cutoff"]
      V --> U["Use source-backed context"]
    end

    subgraph WRITE["Write: source before derived index"]
      direction TB
      C["Sourced candidate learning"] --> X{"Durable and authorized?"}
      X -->|"No"| E["Decline or keep ephemeral"]
      X -->|"Yes"| W["Create or update authoritative domain record"]
      W --> F{"Promote to fleet scope?"}
      F -->|"No"| I["Index immutable domain revision"]
      F -->|"Reviewed approval"| M["Create reviewed fleet-scoped record"]
      M --> I
      I --> Z["Verify source-to-index identity and digest"]
    end

    subgraph RECOVER["Correction and poisoning recovery"]
      direction TB
      B["Bad, stale, or overexposed memory"] --> N["Narrow retrieval and identify affected revisions"]
      N --> R["Correct, supersede, quarantine, or delete source"]
      R --> O["Commit minimized authoritative tombstone or revocation"]
      O --> P2["Verify deletion propagation across supported surfaces"]
      P2 --> G["Build fresh index from pinned sources plus active tombstones"]
      G --> H["Compare source and index manifests; run isolation regressions"]
      H --> J{"Zero unexplained drift?"}
      J -->|"No"| G
      J -->|"Yes"| Y["Atomically promote verified index"]
    end

    U -. "verified lesson candidate" .-> C
    Z -. "later correction" .-> B
